Cell["\<\
This tech note explains how CyclicTagCompiler turns cellular automata and \
automata networks into cyclic tag systems, one simple stage at a time, and \
how to decode the evolution of a cyclic tag system back to the evolution of \
the system it emulates.\
\>", "TechNoteText",
 CellID->906048359,ExpressionUUID->"42ac930b-fb32-194a-bc8d-debe18721302"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction", "TechNoteSection",
 CellID->765158308,ExpressionUUID->"a985388b-8e7c-e54c-81e8-0019f6132ae5"],

Cell["\<\
A cyclic tag system is a very simple system that can nevertheless do any \
computation. This has made cyclic tag systems a useful step in showing that \
other simple systems are universal, such as the rule 110 cellular automaton \
and Wolfram's 2,3 Turing machine.\
\>", "TechNoteText",
 CellID->944594762,ExpressionUUID->"06082448-f06f-d747-ba7a-fbd9a0dec863"],

Cell["\<\
There are three known routes for compiling Turing machines to cyclic tag \
systems. One goes from a Turing machine to a 2-symbol Turing machine, then to \
a tag system and then to a cyclic tag system. Another goes from a 2-symbol \
Turing machine to a Minsky register machine, then to a Fractran program and \
then to a cyclic tag system. Both are fairly simple, but both encode the \
state in unary, so the cyclic tag system is exponentially slower than the \
machine it emulates. The third route goes through clockwise Turing machines \
and avoids the exponential slowdown, but it is much more complicated.\
\>", "TechNoteText",
 CellID->465152263,ExpressionUUID->"b60dd22b-4524-b042-a996-ee1972a56e22"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "CyclicTagCompiler implements a newer route that is both simple and free of \
the exponential slowdown: a cellular automaton or an automata network is \
compiled to an oblivious ring machine, that to an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "9d25fff9-09bd-aa4b-a6f2-47dbdd73a9c9"],
 "-ary cyclic tag system, and that to a cyclic tag system. Each stage is \
short and easy to follow, and none encodes numbers in unary."
}], "TechNoteText",
 CellID->392889331,ExpressionUUID->"43b6149f-d005-1d4a-b870-1a307e6d96a6"],

Cell["\<\
The price is that the systems are finite: a cellular automaton is emulated on \
a cyclic tape of a fixed number of cells. Real computers are finite too, and \
some universality proofs, such as the one for Wolfram's 2,3 Turing machine, \
only need many finite cyclic tag systems, each run for a finite number of \
steps. The other known routes to cyclic tag systems may be added to \
CyclicTagCompiler later.\
\>", "TechNoteText",
 CellID->18461942,ExpressionUUID->"f6645387-376f-5d4c-ab8d-11f3df0e1b65"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The method, including compiling sequential automata networks to oblivious \
ring machines to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "f8265a05-c91c-324c-9de2-bbb9de94abce"],
 "-ary cyclic tag to cyclic tag was worked out by Seth Marshall. Eric James \
Parfitt found the simpler compilation of cellular automata and the \
compilation of more parallel automata networks, and wrote this implementation."
}], "TechNoteText",
 CellID->775356942,ExpressionUUID->"b9433f37-8adb-9548-a77d-8872a26070a6"],

Cell["Load the paclet:", "TechNoteText",
 CellID->679917114,ExpressionUUID->"c4e4bec8-54e7-0b4f-8c0d-2b4249b0ea61"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<EricJamesParfitt`CyclicTagCompiler`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",
 CellID->777064241,ExpressionUUID->"4db1823c-a320-c44c-a895-db2dfa3e5572"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Cyclic Tag Systems", "TechNoteSection",
 CellID->814110646,ExpressionUUID->"6cdc3bb7-77dc-2849-8aa9-6e09a37584e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A cyclic tag system has a tape of 0s and 1s and a list of appendants that \
it uses in turn. At each step it deletes the first cell of the tape, and if \
that cell was 1, it appends the current appendant to the end of the tape. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CyclicTagSystem"]], 
    "paclet:EricJamesParfitt/CyclicTagCompiler/ref/CyclicTagSystem", 
    "EricJamesParfitt Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "625a2cea-2bd3-a64d-aaec-a144622e0dd4"],
 " runs cyclic tag systems:"
}], "TechNoteText",
 CellID->157153821,ExpressionUUID->"fedb1b01-f38e-9942-abee-d4beb0426f80"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run a cyclic tag system with appendants ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "8ce6b6a6-7de5-074f-ba3a-b9fe98daadbd"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "86205e95-6141-7843-9011-68eef57be6ec"],
 " for 6 steps:"
}], "TechNoteMathCaption",
 CellID->428324517,ExpressionUUID->"5e845470-2ee2-9943-89c0-7eae4fca7569"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"CyclicTagSystem", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
